{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1836 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3518c7003dfbdbdbe2c12f8c24f7505a9fbe8b842f69e1b2f86267d5d9f21a25" :edb/db-before-t 1835 :edb/db-after-t 1836 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535148 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:03:50.031Z" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133492 1100 "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3.$ Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/assets/028bb3befd54071fcae6cb88bd3e054d3325557ef31274ec23146e1da81f8258.png)" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133492 1100 "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle = 3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3$. Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle$, if\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535148 false] [17592186133492 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n⟨x, y⟩ &= 3x_{1}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2} + 7x_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-3) + (-2) \\cdot 1 + 7 \\cdot 0 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-9 - 2 + 0 \\\\\n&=-11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 false] [17592186133492 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-9-2+0 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133493 1100 "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n$\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3)$.\nFind $\\langle \\mathbf{x}(t), \\mathbf{y}(t) \\rangle$, if\n${x}(t) = 1-2t+3t^2, \\quad {y}(t) = t-t^2$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186133493 1100 "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\n Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}(t), \\mathbf{y}(t) \\rangle,$ if\n\n$$\n{x}(t) = 1-2t+3t^2,\n\t\\quad\n\t{y}(t) = t-t^2.\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133493 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ &= x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 0 + 9 \\cdot (-2) + 22 \\cdot (-6) \\\\\n&= 0 - 18 - 132 \\\\\n&=-150\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 false] [17592186133493 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+9\\cdot (-2)+22\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =0-18-132 \\\\  & =-150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133494 1100 "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,2\\pi\\right]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,2\\pi\\right]$. Find $\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n$\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{2\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186133494 1100 "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,2\\pi\\right],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,2\\pi\\right].$ Find $\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{2\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133494 1145 "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle  =  \\int_{0}^{2\\pi}\\sin{t} \\cos{t} \\,\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\sin2t =2\\sin t\\cos t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186133494 1145 "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle = \\int_{0}^{2\\pi}\\sin{t} \\cos{t} \\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity\n\n$$\n\\sin2t =2\\sin t\\cos t\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2π}\\sin t\\cos tdt &= \\frac{1}{2}∫_{0}^{2π}\\sin 2tdt \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\\cos 2t \\mid _{0}^{2π} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(\\cos 4π - \\cos 0) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(1 - 1) \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 false] [17592186133685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333846 13194139535148 true] [17592186133685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333874 13194139535148 true] [17592186133685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333888 13194139535148 true] [17592186133685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333902 13194139535148 true] [17592186133686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333853 13194139535148 true] [17592186133686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333860 13194139535148 true] [17592186133686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333895 13194139535148 true] [17592186133687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333867 13194139535148 true] [17592186133687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333881 13194139535148 true] [17592186133687 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333909 13194139535148 true] [17592186134306 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535148 true] [17592186134306 1100 "An inner product on $V = R^{3}$ is given by $⟨x, y⟩ = 2x_{1}y_{1} + x_{2}y_{2} + 9x_{3}y_{3}$. Find $⟨x, y⟩$, if\n\n$x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, y = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186134306 1100 "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+9{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $⟨x,y⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134306 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+9{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot 3+9\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =10-6+9 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134307 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535148 true] [17592186134307 1100 "Let $V = R_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = x(-1)y(-1) + x(0)y(0) + x(1)y(1)$.\nFind $⟨x(t), y(t)⟩$, if\n$x(t) = 5 - 2t + t^{2}, y(t) = t - 1$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186134307 1100 "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)=5-2t+{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=t-1.\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134307 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-16-5+0 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134309 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535148 true] [17592186134309 1100 "Let $V = C[- \\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2}]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[- \\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2}]$. Find $⟨\\sin^{2} t, \\cos t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = ∫_{- π/2}^{π/2}x(t)y(t)dt$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186134309 1100 "Let $V=C[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Find $⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134309 1145 "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134310 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535148 true] [17592186134310 1100 "Let $V = C[0, 2]$, the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0, 2]$. Find $⟨t, e^{t}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$⟨x(t), y(t)⟩ = ∫_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)dt$." 13194139535148 false] [17592186134310 1100 "Let $V=C[0,2],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2].$ Find $⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186134310 1145 "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{t} & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for the integration by parts, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{e}^{2}-0{e}^{0})-{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}-({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333847 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1089 "q-139971" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1100 "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨p,q⟩=2{p}_{1}{q}_{1}+2{p}_{2}{q}_{2}+3{p}_{3}{q}_{3}.$ Find $⟨p,q⟩$, if\n\n$$\np=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1113 #uuid "cc8646fd-56c5-56a3-b836-0c35d2861c86" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333846 1145 "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p,q⟩ & =2{p}_{1}{q}_{1}+2{p}_{2}{q}_{2}+3{p}_{3}{q}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-12-24 \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333848 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333849 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333850 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333851 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333852 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1041 "selection" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333850 13194139535148 true] [17592186333847 1110 #uuid "c87b02d9-f8f1-5ca8-87be-f5ecf40f2530" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333848 1034 "-5" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535148 true] [17592186333848 1111 #uuid "876caeb6-844e-5f64-967b-3f188764a19b" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333849 1034 "15" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535148 true] [17592186333849 1111 #uuid "f27feb54-ef8a-5ed6-8b3b-8352bec9ece0" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333850 1034 "-26" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535148 true] [17592186333850 1111 #uuid "3d0ab54e-4f5d-55a4-a270-39c9bb71a323" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333851 1034 "18" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535148 true] [17592186333851 1111 #uuid "7dcd4b7d-c278-5923-8dfc-e0021261bc88" 13194139535148 true] [17592186333852 1034 "-12" 